2. Character Select — empty slots must not receive hover/focus navigation

The roster currently has 48 slots, with unavailable/empty slots represented by .slot.is-locked.

At the moment those locked slots are still given data-nav, and the shared menu navigator intentionally considers aria-disabled elements focusable. As a result, moving the mouse over an empty slot can move the menu focus/highlight onto it.

Change this behavior so empty/unavailable character slots are non-interactive placeholders.

Requirements:

* Mouse hover must NOT transfer focus/highlight to an empty slot.
* Keyboard/gamepad spatial navigation must skip empty slots.
* Normal Tab navigation must not land on empty slots.
* Empty slots must not show a hover border or focus ring.
* Only actually available fighters should be navigation/selection candidates.
* Preserve the visual empty/locked placeholder grid so the 48-slot roster layout remains intact.
* Do not break future roster expansion: as soon as a character definition is marked available, its slot should behave like a normal selectable fighter without special hard-coded handling for #0001.

A clean implementation is preferred over special-casing the pointer handler. For example, unavailable slots should not receive the same data-nav/focusable interactive markup as available fighters. If keeping them as buttons, ensure they cannot enter focus/navigation; alternatively render unavailable slots as non-interactive elements while preserving the existing .slot.is-locked styling.

Do not globally remove support for disabled navigable elements from menu-navigator.js unless required, because other screens may depend on that behavior.

